   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc15af2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# RQ1: Semantic Entropy and Linguistic Predictors in Clinical Concept Normalisation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Research Question\n",
    "\n",
    "**RQ1:** *Which linguistic properties of meaning-preserving perturbations — perturbation type, magnitude of lexical change, and grammatical category of modified tokens — are the strongest independent predictors of semantic entropy in clinical LLM outputs, and do these predictors interact?*\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the RQ1 pipeline using **MedMentions** as the primary dataset. The dependent variable is **normalised semantic entropy** \\(\\hat{H}(x_0)\\), computed from the distribution of predicted concept clusters over the original input and validated perturbations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Independent variables in the main RQ1 model:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `perturbation_type`\n",
    "- `lexical_change_magnitude`\n",
    "- `linguistic_category`\n",
    "- `perturbation_type × linguistic_category` interaction\n",
    "- `accuracy` (control variable)\n",
    "- `instance_id` and `model_name` as grouping/random factors (mixed-effects target)\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook is designed for reproducible research output generation (tables, figures, CSV files), with a default pilot configuration that can be scaled to full data volume."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2aee292",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
